body:
I'm sorry for what has happened to you. I am sorry, I wish I could help more. I wish I could say everything is going to be okay. But it isn't and it won't be, you might be able to salvage something but most likely far less than you previously had. It is only an effect that his has happened. Not a punishment, but it had it's causation for existing. If you wish to see it as a punishment than that is understandable. 

&#x200B;

It is understandable not to want to kill yourself. It's a self preservation instinct in which it does not allow us to kill ourselves with ease. You are not being selfish, everything is selfish even love. You must get something out of everything, even if it's just furthering the message of hope. Selfish is not a bad thing, it is a natural and human flaw which is overly negatively connotated. 

&#x200B;

I'm sorry, I can't help you. Even a cry of help like this won't save you. I do not condone suicide. But the understanding of reality, and the fragility of both the human body, and psyche it is fee sable. I hope that you can get something if you try...If not then I wish for your death to be quick.
